        "answer": {
          "short": "$8x(x^2+3)^3$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2+3)^4&=4(x^2+3)^3(2x)\\\\&=8x(x^2+3)^3\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p51-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int 8x(x^2+3)^3\\,dx$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x^2+3)^4+C$",
          "worked": "From part a, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2+3)^4=8x(x^2+3)^3$.\n$$\\int 8x(x^2+3)^3\\,dx=(x^2+3)^4+C$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
